    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0370" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.001B14.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Chargé White.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 92.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose, with office copy, a letter
                    addressed by the President to His Excellency Dr. Ramón Báez,<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d349-f1"/> acknowledging the receipt of his letter of August 27 last
                    in which he announced his assumption of the Presidency of the Dominican Republic
                    and his entrance upon the duties of that office.</p>
                <p>You will forward the copy to the Foreign Office and deliver the original in the
                    manner most agreeable to His Excellency.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
